      "score": 89,
      "summary": "Has a clear sequence and a readable findings table with escalation conditions. It handles each HTTP status well, including permissions, idempotency, scoped draft storage and per-item batch retries. Its separation of decisive from contextual signals is excellent. However, it rates the swallowed save error only a conditional P0, which weakens the severity ranking. Its performance budgets are generic field metrics rather than route-specific thresholds, and its fixes have no per-item acceptance conditions."
